[2026-03-15T20:19:09.712Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011638rcCAw1sdpY2r3p4APA","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# netlify-deploy\n     2→\n     3→## Purpose\n     4→\n     5→Safe procedure for running `netlify deploy` in container environments where ANSI escape\n     6→codes and locale issues can corrupt output parsing.\n     7→\n     8→## Procedure\n     9→\n    10→### 1. Strip ANSI codes from output\n    11→\n    12→`netlify deploy` output may contain terminal color codes that corrupt parsed values\n    13→(site IDs, URLs). Always strip ANSI codes before parsing:\n    14→\n    15→```bash\n    16→LC_ALL=C npx netlify deploy --prod --dir dist --functions ./netlify/functions 2>&1 \\\n    17→  | sed 's/\\x1b\\[[0-9;]*m//g' \\\n    18→  | tee logs/deploy-raw.log\n    19→```\n    20→\n    21→Alternatively, use `--json` if the CLI version supports it, which produces\n    22→machine-readable output without ANSI codes.\n    23→\n    24→### 2. Verify the deployed URL\n    25→\n    26→After deployment, confirm the site is reachable before running tests:\n    27→\n    28→```bash\n    29→DEPLOY_URL=\"<extracted-url>\"\n    30→STATUS=$(curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\" \"$DEPLOY_URL\")\n    31→if [ \"$STATUS\" != \"200\" ]; then\n    32→  echo \"ERROR: Site returned $STATUS\"\n    33→fi\n    34→```\n    35→\n    36→### 3. Pre-deploy checklist\n    37→\n    38→Before running `netlify deploy`:\n    39→\n    40→- [ ] `npm run check` passes from the app directory\n    41→- [ ] `vite build` succeeds (check `logs/deploy.log`)\n    42→- [ ] Required env vars are set on Netlify (`DATABASE_URL`, etc.) — use\n    43→  `skills/scripts/netlify-env.md` for the REST API approach\n    44→- [ ] Site ID in `.env` is clean (no embedded ANSI escape sequences)\n    45→- [ ] `LC_ALL=C` is set to prevent locale errors\n    46→\n    47→## Common Issues\n    48→\n    49→- **ANSI-corrupted site ID**: If `.env` contains escape codes in `NETLIFY_SITE_ID`,\n    50→  subsequent `curl` and `netlify` commands fail silently. Re-extract the clean ID from\n    51→  `deployment.txt` or the Netlify dashboard.\n    52→- **502 on first deploy**: Usually caused by missing environment variables on the Netlify\n    53→  site. Set them via the REST API before deploying (see `skills/scripts/netlify-env.md`).\n    54→\n    55→See also: `skills/scripts/deploy.md` for the full deploy script specification.\n    56→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01ET7ubBPVRT5Hd1cLwWoagh","session_id":"e5d16018-2020-41b2-88f2-80c18c9d8446","uuid":"17a48cf7-888c-4648-a790-0839138f58c7"}
