[2026-03-15T20:19:30.688Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ET7ubBPVRT5Hd1cLwWoagh","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a comprehensive understanding. Let me create a summary report.\n\n## Deployment Architecture Summary\n\nBased on my search through the codebase, here's how deployment works in this Google Flights project:\n\n### 1. **Deploy Scripts & Skills**\n\n**Primary Script**: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/deploy.ts`\n- Invoked via: `npm run deploy` (from package.json)\n- Handles the complete deployment pipeline: database setup, schema sync, seeding, Netlify site creation, build, and deploy\n\n**Deployment Skill Documentation**:\n- `/repo/skills/tasks/deployment.md` - Main deployment workflow documentation\n- `/repo/skills/scripts/deploy.md` - Comprehensive deploy script specification\n- `/repo/skills/scripts/netlify-deploy.md` - Safe Netlify CLI procedures\n- `/repo/skills/scripts/deploy-verification.md` - Post-deployment verification steps\n\n### 2. **Netlify Configuration**\n\n**Config File**: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/netlify.toml`\n- Build base: `apps/GoogleFlights`\n- Build command: `npm run build`\n- Publish directory: `dist`\n- Functions path: `netlify/functions`\n- Two redirect rules:\n  - `/api/*` → `/.netlify/functions/:splat` (API routing)\n  - `/*` → `/index.html 200` (SPA routing for client-side routes)\n\n### 3. **Database Seeding in Production**\n\n**Seed Script**: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/seed-db.ts`\n- Exported function: `truncateAndSeed(databaseUrl)`\n- Called automatically on **first deployment only** (line 91-95 in deploy.ts)\n- Flow in deploy.ts:\n  1. Creates Neon database (if new project)\n  2. Syncs schema via `initSchema()`\n  3. On first deploy: calls `truncateAndSeed()` to populate initial data\n  4. Subsequent deploys skip seeding to preserve user data\n\n**What Gets Seeded**:\n- 50 major international airports (IATA codes, coordinates, timezones)\n- 20 airlines with brand colors\n- ~1,250 flights covering:\n  - Major US domestic routes (LAX, JFK, SFO, ORD, etc.)\n  - International routes across Europe, Asia, Middle East, Australia\n  - 31-day SFO→JFK route with 1,050+ flights (for pagination/search testing)\n  - Dynamic pricing based on day-of-week, advance purchase, and random variation\n- Sessions, recent searches, sample bookings, and tracked price routes\n\n**Database Schema** (via `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/schema.ts`):\n- Tables: airports, airlines, flights, flight_legs, prices, sessions, recent_searches, bookings, booking_passengers, tracked_routes\n- Schema is created fresh on each deploy via `initSchema()` (idempotent with `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS`)\n\n### 4. **Deployment.txt Tracking**\n\n**File**: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/deployment.txt`\n- Stores production resource IDs at the top:\n  ```\n  url=<deployed-url>\n  site_id=<netlify-site-id>\n  neon_project_id=<neon-project-id>\n  database_url=<connection-string>\n  ```\n- Preserves deployment history below the resource block\n- Used for redeploying: resource IDs read from here are populated into `.env` to reuse existing infrastructure\n\n**Current Status** (from deployment.txt):\n- Last deployment: 2026-03-15\n- URL: https://google-flights-1773521195043.netlify.app\n- Neon project: rough-firefly-06431753\n- Netlify site: 1518b512-d72f-496d-85ec-00704cbf699d\n\n### 5. **Deployment Steps (Automated)**\n\nThe `deploy.ts` script performs:\n1. **Database Setup** - Create Neon project via API (if new)\n2. **Schema Sync** - Run `initSchema()` to create/update tables\n3. **First-Run Seeding** - Call `truncateAndSeed()` only on initial deployment\n4. **Netlify Site** - Create site via CLI (if new)\n5. **SPA Routing** - Ensure `public/_redirects` exists with SPA rules\n6. **Build** - Run `vite build`\n7. **Deploy** - Run `netlify deploy --prod`\n8. **Persistence** - Write resource IDs to `.env` and `deployment.txt`\n\n### 6. **Key Environment Requirements**\n\nThe deploy script requires three environment variables:\n- `NEON_API_KEY` - For Neon project management\n- `NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN` - For Netlify authentication\n- `NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG` - For site creation\n\nLocale workaround: All Netlify CLI commands prefixed with `LC_ALL=C` to avoid locale errors in containers.\n\n---\n\n**Absolute File Paths**:\n- `/repo/skills/tasks/deployment.md`\n- `/repo/skills/scripts/deploy.md`\n- `/repo/skills/scripts/netlify-deploy.md`\n- `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/deploy.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/seed-db.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/schema.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/netlify.toml`\n- `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/deployment.txt`\n- `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/package.json`"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: aad178748e47d2dcb (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 54923\ntool_uses: 19\nduration_ms: 24533</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e5d16018-2020-41b2-88f2-80c18c9d8446","uuid":"d2fad6ab-3d16-4ea4-8317-e6c64360a8bb","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Find how deployment works in this project. Look for: 1) Any deploy scripts or skills in skills/tasks/, 2) The netlify.toml config, 3) Any seed-db related deployment steps, 4) How the database gets seeded in production. Check skills/tasks/build/ and scripts/ directories. Be quick.","agentId":"aad178748e47d2dcb","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a comprehensive understanding. Let me create a summary report.\n\n## Deployment Architecture Summary\n\nBased on my search through the codebase, here's how deployment works in this Google Flights project:\n\n### 1. **Deploy Scripts & Skills**\n\n**Primary Script**: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/deploy.ts`\n- Invoked via: `npm run deploy` (from package.json)\n- Handles the complete deployment pipeline: database setup, schema sync, seeding, Netlify site creation, build, and deploy\n\n**Deployment Skill Documentation**:\n- `/repo/skills/tasks/deployment.md` - Main deployment workflow documentation\n- `/repo/skills/scripts/deploy.md` - Comprehensive deploy script specification\n- `/repo/skills/scripts/netlify-deploy.md` - Safe Netlify CLI procedures\n- `/repo/skills/scripts/deploy-verification.md` - Post-deployment verification steps\n\n### 2. **Netlify Configuration**\n\n**Config File**: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/netlify.toml`\n- Build base: `apps/GoogleFlights`\n- Build command: `npm run build`\n- Publish directory: `dist`\n- Functions path: `netlify/functions`\n- Two redirect rules:\n  - `/api/*` → `/.netlify/functions/:splat` (API routing)\n  - `/*` → `/index.html 200` (SPA routing for client-side routes)\n\n### 3. **Database Seeding in Production**\n\n**Seed Script**: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/seed-db.ts`\n- Exported function: `truncateAndSeed(databaseUrl)`\n- Called automatically on **first deployment only** (line 91-95 in deploy.ts)\n- Flow in deploy.ts:\n  1. Creates Neon database (if new project)\n  2. Syncs schema via `initSchema()`\n  3. On first deploy: calls `truncateAndSeed()` to populate initial data\n  4. Subsequent deploys skip seeding to preserve user data\n\n**What Gets Seeded**:\n- 50 major international airports (IATA codes, coordinates, timezones)\n- 20 airlines with brand colors\n- ~1,250 flights covering:\n  - Major US domestic routes (LAX, JFK, SFO, ORD, etc.)\n  - International routes across Europe, Asia, Middle East, Australia\n  - 31-day SFO→JFK route with 1,050+ flights (for pagination/search testing)\n  - Dynamic pricing based on day-of-week, advance purchase, and random variation\n- Sessions, recent searches, sample bookings, and tracked price routes\n\n**Database Schema** (via `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/schema.ts`):\n- Tables: airports, airlines, flights, flight_legs, prices, sessions, recent_searches, bookings, booking_passengers, tracked_routes\n- Schema is created fresh on each deploy via `initSchema()` (idempotent with `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS`)\n\n### 4. **Deployment.txt Tracking**\n\n**File**: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/deployment.txt`\n- Stores production resource IDs at the top:\n  ```\n  url=<deployed-url>\n  site_id=<netlify-site-id>\n  neon_project_id=<neon-project-id>\n  database_url=<connection-string>\n  ```\n- Preserves deployment history below the resource block\n- Used for redeploying: resource IDs read from here are populated into `.env` to reuse existing infrastructure\n\n**Current Status** (from deployment.txt):\n- Last deployment: 2026-03-15\n- URL: https://google-flights-1773521195043.netlify.app\n- Neon project: rough-firefly-06431753\n- Netlify site: 1518b512-d72f-496d-85ec-00704cbf699d\n\n### 5. **Deployment Steps (Automated)**\n\nThe `deploy.ts` script performs:\n1. **Database Setup** - Create Neon project via API (if new)\n2. **Schema Sync** - Run `initSchema()` to create/update tables\n3. **First-Run Seeding** - Call `truncateAndSeed()` only on initial deployment\n4. **Netlify Site** - Create site via CLI (if new)\n5. **SPA Routing** - Ensure `public/_redirects` exists with SPA rules\n6. **Build** - Run `vite build`\n7. **Deploy** - Run `netlify deploy --prod`\n8. **Persistence** - Write resource IDs to `.env` and `deployment.txt`\n\n### 6. **Key Environment Requirements**\n\nThe deploy script requires three environment variables:\n- `NEON_API_KEY` - For Neon project management\n- `NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN` - For Netlify authentication\n- `NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG` - For site creation\n\nLocale workaround: All Netlify CLI commands prefixed with `LC_ALL=C` to avoid locale errors in containers.\n\n---\n\n**Absolute File Paths**:\n- `/repo/skills/tasks/deployment.md`\n- `/repo/skills/scripts/deploy.md`\n- `/repo/skills/scripts/netlify-deploy.md`\n- `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/deploy.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/seed-db.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/schema.ts`\n- `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/netlify.toml`\n- `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/deployment.txt`\n- `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/package.json`"}],"totalDurationMs":24533,"totalTokens":54923,"totalToolUseCount":19,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1373,"cache_read_input_tokens":52170,"output_tokens":1373,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1373},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
